Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.24,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,54)\fad(200,0)\fnRoundHog SemiBold\fs34\c&H00B3DA43}Matt Lenhard (Vectoral)
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.24,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,118)\fad(200,0)}“One attack: 100,000
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.24,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,190)\fad(200,0)}requests from 4,000 accounts
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.24,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,262)\fad(200,0)}in 100 milliseconds”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,So for context
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.84,0:00:04.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,we stop like inference
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.30,0:00:06.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,abuse and like token
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.08,0:00:07.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,fraud. So everything
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:08.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,from like CSAM
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.50,0:00:09.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,distillation
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.84,0:00:10.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,cyber attacks being
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.68,0:00:13.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,proxied through AI
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.36,0:00:14.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,endpoints.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.11,0:00:15.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,So we recently saw an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.59,0:00:17.43,Caption,,0,0,0,,attack that was across
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.43,0:00:19.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,probably 3,000
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.15,0:00:21.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,4,000 accounts
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.43,0:00:23.69,Caption,,0,0,0,,100,000 requests all
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.69,0:00:26.35,Caption,,0,0,0,,within 100 milliseconds
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.35,0:00:27.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,and this person had been
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.99,0:00:28.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,sitting on these
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.51,0:00:29.31,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.31,0:00:30.93,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some were bought up from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.93,0:00:32.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,the underground markets
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.51,0:00:33.37,Caption,,0,0,0,,some were probably spun
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.37,0:00:34.39,Caption,,0,0,0,,up from automation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.39,0:00:36.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,But it shows you...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.79,0:00:38.09,Caption,,0,0,0,,I guess with the power
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.09,0:00:39.55,Caption,,0,0,0,,of AI, what's possible
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.55,0:00:41.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,where an attack can now
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.07,0:00:43.31,Caption,,0,0,0,,be, if they just want a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.31,0:00:44.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,few things to slip
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.17,0:00:45.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,through, it might be a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.65,0:00:46.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,million requests across
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.97,0:00:48.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,a large number of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.11,0:00:50.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.51,0:00:52.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,We think of it really as
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.73,0:00:54.47,Caption,,0,0,0,,anomaly detection.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.47,0:00:56.39,Caption,,0,0,0,,Can you, specifically in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.39,0:00:57.89,Caption,,0,0,0,,terms of endpoint
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.89,0:00:58.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,security
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.65,0:01:00.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,can you detect
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.11,0:01:01.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,anomalies?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.27,0:01:03.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,across a large number of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.65,0:01:06.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts extremely fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.06,0:01:06.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,It's a hard problem
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.98,0:01:08.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,like how do you roll up
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.18,0:01:09.66,Caption,,0,0,0,,if you've got 100,000
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.66,0:01:10.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,requests coming in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.60,0:01:11.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,how do you roll up
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.32,0:01:12.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,what's normal for those
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.52,0:01:15.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts all at once in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.08,0:01:16.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,milliseconds?
